{"base_manifest_sha256":"531f85386978d805de3756d2d1c70d748a4cd392c0caad3c4173e8a9d9c6fa06","review":{"basis":"Pinned per-version reference records and explicit bounded reconstruction; not TradingView execution proof.","date":"2026-10-23","decisions":["Flat products contain 2..16 resolved scalar results. They are ephemeral return values, not first-class arrays or mutable tuple variables. Each result inherits the strongest dependency qualifier.","Destructuring declares new scalar names atomically after exactly one evaluation; repeated underscore targets discard values. UDF returns and explicit value-if branches share the same representation. Nested products, tuple parameters, tuple reassignment and tuple ternary are excluded.","MACD is recorded in v1..v6; the legacy array spelling is interpreted as a fixed three-result product. BB has no v1..v3 reference and is explicitly reconstructed there from SMA and population standard deviation.","Variance/stdev use a fixed simple-int length 1..100000, last length defined sources, full warmup and exact binary sums/squares. Unbiased singleton yields NA. Optional biased=true is admitted only in v5/v6, matching their reference signatures.","MACD reuses the existing version-specific EMA accumulators: SMA seed before v5, first defined source in v5/v6. On missing source fast/slow hold; the signal still consumes a defined difference. Each written composite call owns one complete checkpoint/rollback state.","BB returns mean, mean+mult*population-stdev and mean-mult*population-stdev. Nonpositive or missing multipliers are not replaced silently.","One unconditional request may return a flat numeric product from the admitted expression subset. All components share one requested evaluation, event, gaps/lookahead mapping and checkpoint. UDF captures, nested/dynamic requests and lower timeframes remain excluded."],"external_pine_execution":false,"test_refs":["tests/test_composite.py","tests/test_composite_state.py","tests/test_composite_pipel